text:
DICAEOPOLIS
Not Phoenix, no;
there was another, more wretched than Phoenix.

DICAEOPOLIS
By no means, Lamachus;
for this isn't a matter of strength. And if you're strong,
why didn't you circumcise me? You're well-armed enough.

DICAEOPOLIS
It looks like a piglet now;
but when it's grown it'll be a cunt.

MEGARIAN
But they didn't gobble down all the figs;
for I picked up this one of them myself.

BOEOTIAN
By Iolaus, you do me a kindness there, stranger;
for, blowing from Thebes behind me,
they've shaken the blossoms off my pennyroyal onto the ground.
But buy, if you like, some of what I'm carrying,
some of the chicks or the four-winged things.

BRIDESMAN
The bridesmaid;
she wants to say something to you, from the bride, in private.
